This project is derived from Caduceus for the E-P7 (https://github.com/cakelesscoder/caduceus-ep7, Copyright 2026
cakelesscoder, Apache-2.0); it is not a fork on GitHub and does not carry its history. Files from that project are kept
here with changes: the build and package tools (caduceus.py,
tools/build_package.py, tools/osd_extract.py, ...), the patch modules patches/buttons, patches/omc_buttons,
patches/btn_arrows, patches/lcd_tint, patches/fw_version and the assembler helpers they call (patches/sd_bundles*),
the documents in docs/ that come from that project, and releases/v0.29a/edits.json, kept only as a reference for the checks
of the final build. The other upstream features (film looks, look editor, EP7MOD loader, grain, aspect, Control Panel, ...) were
removed from this project. Modules added by this project: patches/lever_nomenu, patches/jpeg_always, patches/final,
tools/fork_build.py, docs/FINAL_BUILD.md, docs/JPEG_ALWAYS.md.

This repository contains no Olympus / OM Digital Solutions firmware. The build downloads the official firmware from
OM's own server on the user's machine and checks its SHA-256.

Third-party:
- external/oly_fw_analysis (git submodule, fishcu, https://github.com/fishcu/oly_fw_analysis): PEN-F firmware research and MN103
  emulator harness, used by the verification tools only. It keeps its own licence (GPL-3.0 for its code) and is not part of
  this firmware.

